BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Woods Walk: Weeks Memorial Forest
DTSTART:20260929T100000
DTEND:20260929T113000
DTSTAMP:20260928T183908Z
UID:54b3bfc315af5932597b198324be0c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join New England Forestry Foundation (NEFF) for a scenic and i
 mmersive woods walk through the soon-to-be harvested Weeks Memorial Forest
  in Guilford\, Vermont\, where you’ll learn about sustainable\, climate-
 smart forestry! This approximately 1.5-hour guided hike will offer an in-d
 epth look at Exemplary Forestry practices\, with a focus on controlling in
 vasive species and improving biodiversity. Ask questions\, explore the lan
 dscape\, and discover how NEFF is shaping the future of New England’s fo
 rests. This event will take place rain or shine. Please register below if 
 you plan to attend. What to Expect —Moderate Hike: 1 to 1.5 miles throug
 h varying terrain\, including well-worn trails\, exposed roots\, branches
 \, and rocks —Sustained Grades: The hike will include prolonged inclines
  of up to 10 percent —Expert Guidance: A licensed forester will explain 
 sustainable\, climate-smart harvesting techniques and answer questions Who
  Should Participate? This moderate hike requires participants to be in goo
 d physical health and capable of: —Walking up to 1.5 miles over uneven t
 errain —Navigating rocks\, roots\, and other natural obstacles —Managi
 ng sustained inclines of up to 10 percent grade What to Bring —Long pant
 s and appropriate clothing (hat\, comfortable hiking boots or shoes) —In
 sect repellent (DEET or similar recommended for ticks and mosquitoes) —W
 ater and snacks (if desired) —Medically necessary items (EpiPen\, inhale
 r\, etc.) Children of all ages are welcome but must be supervised. Arrive 
 10–15 minutes early at the designated parking lot. Registrants are encou
 raged to download a trail map and GPS directions for the parking lot in ad
 vance. Weeks Memorial Forest\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fall-woods
 -walk-weeks-memorial-forest-11-09-2026-12-56-25
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vermont Agriculture: A Renaissance of the Past
DTSTART:20260929T170000
DTEND:20260929T190000
DTSTAMP:20260928T183908Z
UID:bb09db9b0ec52934ac7289916d2792@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Samuel Hand Lecture will feature a talk from former V
 ermont Secretary of Agriculture Roger Allbee drawing on the research for h
 is 2025 book\, Turning the Soil: 250 Years of Vermont Agriculture. Hearty 
 refreshments to follow. Turning the Soil: 250 Years of Vermont Agriculture
  by Roger Allbee traces Vermont’s farming history from before statehood 
 to the present\, emphasizing that the only constant has been change. Allbe
 e grew up on his family’s hillside dairy farm in the Vermont town his an
 cestors settled\, where they have farmed continuously since 1794\; though 
 not a farmer by trade\, that deep roots and his later policy roles (Vermon
 t Secretary of Agriculture\; USDA Farm Service Agency executive director) 
 shape the book’s perspective. The book moves through key turning points
 —early mixed farming\, the 19th‑century sheep boom and bust\, the rise
  of dairy and maple\, and the impact of westward expansion\, technology\, 
 policy\, and markets—to show how farmers repeatedly reinvented their ent
 erprises. Blending stories of individual farmers and leaders with broader 
 historical forces\, it argues that these cycles of adaptation are Vermont
 ’s agricultural heritage and a roadmap for the future. UVM Billings Libr
 ary\, Marsh Room\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/vermont-ag
 riculture-a-renaissance-of-the-past-02-09-2026-14-08-11
END:VEVENT
